          "On 1 July Hadrian watched the legion’s exercises on the Lambaesis parade ground and addressed the soldiers group by group: the officers of the first centuries, the legionary cavalry and the infantry units. His words are detailed professional critiques: he praises the quick building of ramparts and the accurate javelin throwing, the horsemen’s skill in vaulting onto their horses, and elsewhere urges caution. He also mentions that several units of the legion had been detached elsewhere, yet it had performed excellently.\n\n"
